# Supabase migrations – confirmation

When you **create a new migration file** in `supabase/migrations/`:

1. **Do not assume** the new migration (or any migration) has been applied to the database.
2. **Ask the user** to confirm whether they have run migrations, and which ones (e.g. “Have you run the migrations up to 042? Please run `supabase db push` or apply the new migration, then confirm.”).
3. Only give instructions that rely on the new migration being applied **after** the user confirms they have run it (or after they say they will run it).

When **editing an existing migration** that the user says they have **not** yet run, it is safe to change that migration; still remind them to run it and ask for confirmation once done.
